message.content:
Dog sweaters and similar pet apparel are classified in HTSUS 4201, "Saddlery and harness for any animal (including traces, leads, knee pads, muzzles, saddle cloths, saddle bags, dog coats and the like), of any material." Dog coats are named there, and CBP rulings have placed dog sweaters and hoodies in 4201.00.60 as "other" (not of leather). Chapter 61 does not apply because Note 1 to Section XI/Chapter 61 limits it to garments for humans, and the pet apparel is covered by 4201.

The statistical suffix is the part I am less sure of. 4201.00.60 is the subheading for articles of other materials, and I recall its suffix as 00. HTSUS 4201.00.60 is "Other" with statistical suffix 00, giving 4201.00.6000.

{"hts_code": "4201.00.6000", "reason": "Dog sweaters and hoodies are pet apparel ('dog coats and the like') classified in heading 4201 as saddlery and harness for animals, of materials other than leather."}
